      "derivation": "Age PMF=normal cell masses conditional34.5<=age*<=74.5. BMI log_mu=log(reported median), log_sd=log(q75/q25)/(2*Phi^-1(.75)); this fits median+quartile ratio, not both asymmetric endpoints. Shifted positive law s^2=log(1+(sd/(mean-floor))^2), mu=log(mean-floor)-s^2/2. r_latent(H,G)=2*sin(pi*rho_S/6). r_latent(B,H)=log(1+r_P*sqrt(expm1(sB^2)*expm1(sH^2)))/(sB*sH). Age-BMI=.10,age-glucose=.20,BMI-glucose=.25 are assumptions. Age-H correlation solves exact discrete-age/shifted-lognormal covariance identity for within-sex OLS age=.010, with90 deterministic bisection steps; formula and precision in static_model_math.py/report. All other entries are numerical derivations of these choices, not extra source estimates."
    },
